      "side": 1,
      "message": "After this CL, the existing dependency edge from `//rust/png:ffi_rs` to `//rust/common:skia_rust_common` (and the new edge to `//rust/common:cxx_bridge`) becomes actually used/needed by `rust/png/FFI.rs`.  So, we probably need to tweak a few things here to make sure that the artifacts/results of the Bazel build are propagated into Skia\u0027s GN/ninja build.\n\nI think that for simplicity it\u0027s okay to cover *both* `//rust/png` and `//rust/common` inside the same targets (keeping the target names for now).\n\n------------------------------\n\nLet me try to share a broader context - I hope this helps.\n\nI understand that having to support multiple build environments leads to quite a few complications.  I wish that we could go back in time and just use Bazel for Chromium and Skia (IIUC Bazel wasn\u0027t ready for OSS back when Chromium was deciding whether to invest in GN/ninja).  But we\u0027re here, and this is what we have to deal with :-/.\n\nOn Skia-side, the goals are:\n\n1. Ensure that Bazel build works fine.  It seems that this may already work after this CL, but I am mentioning this here for completeness.   (Can also build `//tools:full_build` target for more coverage/assurance; both the narrow and broader build targets will transitively cover `//rust/png` and [after this CL] `//rust/common`).  \n\n    ```\n    $ cd third_party/skia/\n    $ bazelisk build //:png_decode_rust //:png_encode_rust\n    ```\n\n2. Ensure that GN/ninja build works fine.  I think that this part may be broken (because there are no changes between new lines 1447-1522.  GN/ninja build in Skia (unlike in Chromium) doesn\u0027t support Rust - for building Rust it delegates to Bazel (as described in this comment).  I wrote this piece of `BUILD.gn` but the precedence for this approach is Fontations (which has a similar piece elsewhere in this `BUILD.gn`).\n\n    ```\n    $ #optional?: python3 tools/git-sync-deps\n    $ cat out/args.gn\n    # A bit random / just what I happen to use on my machine at the moment.\n    cc \u003d \"clang\"\n    cxx \u003d \"clang++\"\n    \n    skia_build_fuzzers \u003d true\n    \n    skia_use_fontations \u003d false\n    skia_use_rust_png_decode \u003d true\n    skia_use_rust_png_encode \u003d true\n    skia_use_libpng_decode \u003d false\n    skia_use_libpng_encode \u003d true\n    \n    $ autoninja -C out dm # build tests that (among other things) cover Rust PNG decoding/encoding\n    ```\n    \n3. Make sure that Chromium build works fine when combined with the Skia CL.  I think you have already verified this, so only mentioning this for completeness.",
